I'll analyze the file and identify methods that need to be updated to send the whole message object instead of just the changed field.

## Analysis

Methods that need updating:
1. `toggleHide()` - sends only `{ doc_id, hide }`
2. `toggleAnswer()` - sends only `{ doc_id, is_answer }`

These methods should fetch the full message object, update the specific field, and send the entire message.

## Changes

```js src/service/chat.js
  async toggleHide({ chat, doc_id }) {
    if (!chat?.id || !doc_id) {
      return
    }

    const msg = chat.messages.find((m) => m.doc_id === doc_id)
    if (!msg) return

    const newHideValue = !msg.hide
    return await this.$storex.chats.updateMessage({ 
      chat, 
      message: { 
        ...msg,
        hide: newHideValue 
      }
    })
  }

  async toggleAnswer({ chat, doc_id }) {
    if (!chat?.id || !doc_id) {
      return
    }

    const msg = chat.messages.find((m) => m.doc_id === doc_id)
    if (!msg) return

    const newAnswerValue = !msg.is_answer
    return await this.$storex.chats.updateMessage({ 
      chat, 
      message: { 
        ...msg,
        is_answer: newAnswerValue 
      }
    })
  }
```

## Summary of changes

| Method | Change |
|--------|--------|
| `toggleHide()` | Now spreads full message object (`...msg`) before updating `hide` field |
| `toggleAnswer()` | Now spreads full message object (`...msg`) before updating `is_answer` field |

This ensures the complete message object is sent to the update operation, preventing accidental deletion of other message fields.

